# Prose numbers that are legitimately not experiment results.
# One per line, with a reason. A growing file here is a smell — it usually means
# results that should be logged are not being logged.

# --- dataset and task constants, not measurements ---
28      # image side length in pixels, from MNIST
784     # 28 x 28, the flattened image length
392     # 28 x 14, hidden pixels per query at the default mask
255     # uint8 pixel maximum, the divisor that puts pixels in [0,1]
70      # first half of "70 000", the MNIST total
60      # first half of "60 000", the MNIST training split size
0.0625  # 1/16, the derived chance level for identification at M=16

# --- digit-grouped numerals the checker splits on the thin space ---
# Typst renders these with a space inside the numeral ("16 384"), so the linter
# sees two tokens. The leading group matches a real value; the trailing one
# cannot.
384     # trailing group of "16 384", the state size (H x dk x dk = 4 x 64 x 64)
544     # trailing group of "12 544", context content at M=16 (16 x 784)
704     # trailing group of "200 704", context content at M=256 (256 x 784)
176     # trailing group of "50 176", context content at M=64 (64 x 784)
136     # trailing group of "3 136", context content at M=4 (4 x 784)
192     # trailing group of "8 192", state size at dk=32
096     # trailing group of "4 096", state size at dk=16
048     # trailing group of "2 048", state size at dk=8
000     # trailing group of "12 000" (steps), "60 000" / "70 000" (dataset)

# --- optimiser and reporting constants ---
300     # learning-rate warm-up steps
80      # "80% more per step", a wall-clock observation not stored in results

# (The block of `gain` values that used to sit here is gone: the paper now quotes
# conditions B and D as measured rather than their difference, so every number in
# it is a stored one. A shrinking allow-list is the point of the mechanism.)

# --- hardware ---
4090    # the GPU model number

# --- values that live in `history`, which the numeric lint does not read ---
# The check walks each row's `final` block (655 values); the per-evaluation
# curves are not in that pool, so "best over training" numbers and any curve
# value quoted at a particular step land here. `lib/train.py` now also logs
# `gain` and `best_nmse` per row, so runs from this point on will match
# directly and these entries can be retired as the old rows are superseded.
0.635   # exp1 best D, and its D at step 500
0.380   # exp1 A at step 500
0.803   # exp1 D at step 2000
0.777   # exp6 best D
0.535   # exp4 best D
0.443   # exp5 best D
0.458   # exp2 and exp12 best D
0.459   # exp3 best D
0.450   # exp7 best D
b2303c6 # superseded commit hash from an earlier appendix revision
122bb8c # ditto
